 "dyld_hand_read_observations": [
  {
   "not_established": "where the allocator byte at +0x21 is set to non-zero (no strb of a non-zero constant to a +0x21 field was found in the allocator code; the origin may be a wider store); nothing here says which path an S24 run takes",
   "reads": "a byte at offset 0x21 of an allocator object reached through offset 0x60 of the function's receiver; when it is non-zero dyld reads the commpage byte at +0x10c, jumps to a `brk #1` (0x7d3c) if it is 0, or if (byte & 0xfe) != 2; then `mrs x8, S3_6_C15_C1_5`, loads the commpage u64 at +0xd0, `msr S3_6_C15_C1_5` with it, `isb`, loads +0xd0 again, `mrs` again and `brk`s if the two differ.  The twin sequence at 0x7bb0 uses +0xd8.",
   "when_the_byte_is_zero": "the same function takes the branch at 0x7980 to 0x7a20 and uses lsl::MemoryManager::lockGuard and mprotect-style write protection (MemoryManager::writeProtect issues ___mprotect with PROT_READ=1 and PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE=3)",
   "where": "dyld4::APIs::dlopen_from, vm 0x7980-0x7a1c and 0x7bb0 onwards (symbol-table label; the cold-path calls at 0x7d30-0x7d38 belong to it)"
  },
  {
   "reads": "the commpage u64 at +0x160 (dyld_system_flags) and writes it through sysctlbyname(\"kern.dyld_flags\", ..., 8)",
   "ties_to": "the project kernel declares _COMM_PAGE_DYLD_FLAGS at +0x160 and the sysctl kern.dyld_flags (see sysctl_source_review)",
   "where": "dyld4::SyscallDelegate::dyldCommPageFlags / setDyldCommPageFlags, vm 0x30260-0x302a4"
  }
 ],
